{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ve found several plan-level contradictions, not just missing implementation detail: the generic resolver cannot perform the promised cursor write-back as currently specified; bounded rounds have no progress rule for entries beyond the budget; and W3’s queue/timer disposition path is an out-of-band control mechanism that conflicts with the stated no-callback/no-shared-mutation boundary. I’m completing the evidence map and separating those from smaller schema/test gaps."}}
